cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its measurements in academic work, please cite it.
  Citation is requested, not required by the license.
title: "Seed — a research instrument for measuring agent initiative"
abstract: >-
  A generative-TTRPG engine repurposed as a measurement instrument for the
  question "when should an agent act without being asked?". World state is a
  fold over a typed delta log under a single writer with seeded RNG, which
  yields machine-checkable ground-truth belief state, information asymmetry as
  a tunable parameter, and exact counterfactual replay — forking a turn into
  agent-acts and agent-stays-silent branches and reading the outcome difference
  off the world model.
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Runkai
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
# version, date-released, doi and repository-code are filled in at the first
